A database through four releases, as a team's work reaches it:

1. Release 2: `title` renamed `name` (a @drop and a @from).
2. Release 3, a teammate's branch merged after: a `note` column. The
   rename's lines, of release 2, are history to a database at 2.
3. Release 4: a UNIQUE added on `name`: a rebuild, the rows copied by name.
4. Release 5: the rename's lines removed, and `@oldest 3` says so.

Each deploy plans only its own change; the rows survive all four. The
database starts at release 1.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup', 95), (2, 'bread', 40);
PRAGMA user_version = 1;

== after
-- @release 2
-- @drop 2 column dish title
-- @from 2 column dish name = title
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;

== after
-- @release 3
-- @drop 2 column dish title
-- @from 2 column dish name = title
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;

== after
-- @release 4
-- @drop 2 column dish title
-- @from 2 column dish name = title
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;

== after
-- @release 5
-- @oldest 3
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;

== query
SELECT id, name, price_kr, note FROM dish ORDER BY id

== plan
